# Copy to app/.env.local for local development.
# In CI these come from GitHub repository variables, not this file.

# Archival/paid RPC. The public endpoint returns 403 to browsers, so the
# dashboard will not load against it.
#
# The production key is domain-locked at Helius to mybestbuddy.fun and
# www.mybestbuddy.fun — it has to be, because a VITE_ variable is compiled into
# the public JS bundle and anyone can read it there. Requests from any other
# Origin get "Forbidden".
#
# Helius rejects "localhost" as an allowed-domain value, so http://localhost:5173
# can never be allowlisted. Instead of weakening the key with a second
# unrestricted copy, reach the dev server through our permanent ngrok domain,
# which *is* allowlisted:
#
#   Terminal 1:  npm run dev        (repo root or app/)
#   Terminal 2:  npm run tunnel     (repo root or app/)
#   Open:        https://ryleigh-companyless-outbully.ngrok-free.dev
#
# Open that URL, not localhost — the Origin header is what Helius checks. See
# docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md "Local development against mainnet".
VITE_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY

# The deployed distributor program.
VITE_PROGRAM_ID=7h8fAnCmpeLaAo2Y9j43wrdERexUycMH5CV484v5wtrP

# The only hostname this build should be served on. Firebase always also serves
# <site-id>.web.app and there is no way to disable that, so the app redirects
# those to here. Leave unset locally.
VITE_CANONICAL_HOST=mybestbuddy.fun
